  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>Leptobarbus hoevenii, the Cigar Shark or Mad Barb, is a giant among the barbs. With a length of approx. 1 m and a weight of up to 10 kg it needs a lot of space.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>They originate from Southeast Asia (Thailand to Borneo).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are found most often in freely flowing rivers and streams and seasonally on floodplains.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>For the maintenance of adults one should own a tank of at least 3 m length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>In terms of water chemistry they place no special requirements.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>As omnivorous fish they are unproblematic in their nutrition.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>Since they are schooling fish, one should keep a group of at least 7 individuals, which can form a magnificent swarm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/leptobarbus_hoevenii_en/",
      "html": "<p>Nothing is known about breeding in aquariums. In Asia they are artificially bred for raising in aquacultures.</p>"
    }
  ],
